Fix an integer $d\ge2$ and a macro width $0<h<1$. After starting at a sufficiently late macro endpoint, there is a grid $s_k	o\infty$ with macro endpoints $S_j=e^{hj}$ and the following properties. Each macro interval is either one bad step or is divided into regular steps of length comparable to $\sqrt{S_j}$. Thus, eventually,  egin{equation} c_h\sqrt{s_k}\le\Delta s_k:=s_{k+1}-s_k \le(e^h-1)s_k. \end{equation} For $F_k=F_{s_k,s_{k+1}}$ there are polynomial local coordinate changes $H_k$ and polynomial automorphisms $G_k$ of $\C^n$ satisfying  egin{equation} J_d(H_{k+1}\circ F_k)=J_d(G_k\circ H_k). \end{equation} The degrees of $H_k,G_k,G_k^{-1}$ are bounded independently of $k$. The coefficients of $H_k$ and its inverse jet are $\exp(o(s_k))$; $H_k'(0)$ and its inverse have polynomial bounds in $s_k$. For a constant $C_d$ depending only on the fixed jet order and dimension,  egin{align} 
orm{G_k}_{\mathrm{coeff}}+
orm{G_k^{-1}}_{\mathrm{coeff}} &\le \exp igl(C_d\Delta s_k+o(s_k) igr), \ 
orm{G_k'(0)^{-1}} &\le s_k^{C}\exp(\Delta s_k/2). \end{align} In particular, the coefficient $C_d$ of $\Delta s_k$ is independent of $h$. Finally, for some finite $D$,  egin{equation} \deg G_{0,k}\le D s_k \quad	ext{on an unbounded subsequence of macro endpoints.} \end{equation}
